I think there is still an issue that we're not handling all the promises in `popupLookups` in the first tick, as you're `await`ing in a loop. Perhaps we can just combine everything into the initial promise:

```javascript
const result = [];
const popupLookups = cmps.map(cmp => this.waitForPopup(cmp).then((isOpen) => {
  if (isOpen) result.push(cmp)
}).catch(() => {}); 
// As we've silence errors, we can safely use `Promise.all`
await Promise.all(popupLookup);
return result;
```

Alternatively, if we want to be as fast as possible, we could turn `detectPopups` into an async generator, and use `Promise.race` to emit the first open popup ASAP.

