[nitpick] The `__oldStyles` property isn’t declared on `HTMLElement`. Extend the `HTMLElement` interface or use a `WeakMap`/symbol to store previous styles and avoid TypeScript errors.
```suggestion
const oldStylesMap = new WeakMap<HTMLElement, string>();

export function highlightNode(node: HTMLElement) {
    if (!node.style) return;
    if (oldStylesMap.has(node)) {
        return; // already highlighted
    }
    if (node.hasAttribute('style')) {
        oldStylesMap.set(node, node.style.cssText);
```

